#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Run a canonical CSG test list under an exact 1 GiB process-tree cap.

The Linux authority is the repository's native cgroup-v2 runner. It attaches
the command root before exec, so every descendant inherits the same aggregate
memory.max. An aggregate OOM control is required before any CSG command runs.

Darwin has no repository-bound kernel or VM aggregate-memory authority. A
Darwin invocation therefore writes a sealed hard-red receipt and exits nonzero.
User-space RSS sampling and per-process rlimits are never proof authorities.
"""

